build/
.ported-state.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Vendored hyprsaver source tree at vendor/hyprsaver. Upstream includes
# `/target/` (cargo build outputs — irrelevant since we build with our own
# `tools/build-hyprsaver.sh`), `examples/palettes/` (auto-generated at
# build-time from build.rs), and `media/` (animated webp preview GIF-
# equivalents used by the upstream README galleries — marketing, not
# source). Also excluded are upstream-only authorial / distro-packaging
# artifacts (CLAUDE.md, the AUR PKGBUILD, the nix flake, deny.toml,
# rustfmt.toml, .github/) that aren't relevant when hyprsaver is
# consumed as a vendored library rather than as its own project.
#
# The remaining vendored tree is the source of record: Cargo.toml,
# Cargo.lock, src/, shaders/, build.rs, README.md, LICENSE (MIT,
# retained unmodified), CHANGELOG.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/, examples/.
vendor/hyprsaver/target/
vendor/hyprsaver/examples/palettes/
vendor/hyprsaver/media/
vendor/hyprsaver/CLAUDE.md
vendor/hyprsaver/PKGBUILD
vendor/hyprsaver/flake.nix
vendor/hyprsaver/flake.lock
vendor/hyprsaver/deny.toml
vendor/hyprsaver/rustfmt.toml
vendor/hyprsaver/.github/
